+### Architecture Overview
+
+Haive is a modular AI agent framework with the following key packages:
+- **haive-core**: Core engine, state management, tools, and infrastructure
+- **haive-agents**: Pre-built agent implementations (RAG, ReAct, Multi-agent, etc.)
+- **haive-tools**: Tool integrations and toolkits
+- **haive-games**: Game environments and agents  
+- **haive-dataflow**: Streaming and data processing with Supabase integration
+- **haive-mcp**: Model Context Protocol integration
+- **haive-prebuilt**: Ready-to-use agent configurations
+
+### Key Directories
+- **Packages**: `/home/will/Projects/haive/backend/haive/packages/`
+- **Tests**: `packages/{package_name}/tests/`  
+- **Documentation**: `/project_docs/` for development docs, `/docs/source/` for user docs
+
+## Development Patterns
+
+### Agent Creation
+```python
+from haive.agents.simple.agent import SimpleAgent
+from haive.core.engine.aug_llm import AugLLMConfig
+
+# Create basic agent with Supabase auto-persistence
+engine = AugLLMConfig()
+agent = SimpleAgent(engine=engine, name="MyAgent")
+
+# Run with conversation persistence
+result = agent.run(
+    {'messages': [HumanMessage(content="Hello!")]},
+    config={'configurable': {'thread_id': 'unique-conversation-id'}}
+)
+```
+
+### Multi-Agent Systems
+```python
+from haive.agents.multi.agent import MultiAgent
+
+# Multi-agent with shared state
+multi_agent = MultiAgent(
+    agents=[agent1, agent2],
+    coordination_strategy="sequential"
+)
+```
 
